# A0: the FIRST job of the window. Production is LIVE on the four cards: this stops the node agent (and with it the serving container it
# started) and removes the placement's serving state, so the cards are free. It opens no card. Pass: no serving container and
# no holder of the four boards. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (nothing below may open a card under a live endpoint).
# Duration (estimate): 10 min.
# No status action: the driver would flag production's container as stale. The placement record stays in the platform; the DRIVER hands the cards back at the end of
# the window (all-four reset, fabric re-measure, agentstart): no job of this pack does, so no job can bring the node agent back mid-programme.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sdpa-long window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sdpa-long and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a
# card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a is a PLACEHOLDER for an image on the rig that carries the K64j op graft: the driver CONFIRMS it BEFORE this job
# runs (IMAGE_CHECK_ONLY=1 in the Q1 harness; see ORDER.txt step P1) and substitutes it in every template if it is another;
# no build job is needed because the sweep mounts its scripts from the checkout and the serving flag is not exercised here.
# PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when the window opens: A0 is the first job and the only one that takes it down.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=agentstop unserve
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
